    {
      "id": "claim_82020b842a744dd28a947f87aec24618",
      "statement": "The porting rule of thumb: if a file talks to the network or computes a token, call @ulabase/kit instead of writing it; if a file describes what a screen looks like, copy it — only the glue between them is genuinely new work. Ports must also rebuild an HTTP layer that attaches the bearer token and clears the session on 401/expiry, and scheduleRefresh() from the kit (15-minute token TTL, silently renewed at ~80%).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://PORTING.md#L28-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37871c39f1843a107c6ae6b277e32a10878c7b74ded73f3ea8ce9fd11b540b56:"
